    "text_result": "I've read the actual `diff base \u2192 merge commit` diff for every file in the changeset and written the JSON response.\n\nKey findings from the diffs:\n\n- **WiredTiger error-code migration** (the substantive change): statistics-cursor failures now flow through `wtRCToStatus` instead of being hardcoded to `CursorNotFound`, yielding `NoSuchKey` (missing file) or `ObjectIsBusy` (held data handle). `wiredtiger_util.cpp`, `wiredtiger_kv_engine.cpp` (with a new `WTIndexStorageSizeReturnBusy` failpoint), and `wiredtiger_util_test.cpp` are all updated consistently.\n- **Bazel coverage plumbing** in `resmoke.bzl` (cc toolchain env, LLVM profile file override, `llvm_coverage_dso` transition).\n- Minor build/config/doc updates, a heartbeat-interval tweak in `replicaset.py`, removal of an unused constant in `replication_coordinator_impl.cpp`, and comment-only additions in `wiredtiger.h.in`.\n- The two conflict files (`MODULE.bazel.lock`, `sbom.json`) described per the fork's resolution policy.\n\nEvery symbol and behavior stated in the response is backed by lines present in the diffs I read.",
    "response": {
      "summary": "Merges upstream MongoDB changes into the fork. The main functional change is in the WiredTiger storage layer: statistics-cursor open failures are no longer flattened into ErrorCodes::CursorNotFound but are now mapped through wtRCToStatus, so a missing file surfaces as NoSuchKey and a transiently held data handle surfaces as ObjectIsBusy. Callers are updated accordingly: getIdentSize/getEphemeralIdentSize treat both NoSuchKey and ObjectIsBusy as a zero-size (gone) ident, while getIndexStorageSize treats NoSuchKey as zero-contribution and propagates ObjectIsBusy so the caller can retry, aided by a new WTIndexStorageSizeReturnBusy failpoint. The merge also brings Bazel coverage plumbing for resmoke server binaries, several build-config and doc updates, a resmoke replica-set heartbeat-interval tweak, and WiredTiger header comment additions. Conflicts in MODULE.bazel.lock and sbom.json were resolved.",
